# Sentence 1 of Babelingua's demonstration (video, 14:39), post-4D-movement.
# 'Never, from the far past onward, have I comprehended it: the allure of Aghma Shwa'
#
# Back-transcribed from the IPA shown on screen, e.g. [ʔələwəqjəm] = אלוקים,
# [fəðəv] = פדב, [həħəm] = החם (5+8+600 = 613). A dagesh (ּ) marks the few
# places where the demo uses a hard stop, like [ħəkəz] = חכּז.
# The demo itself breaks some of its own rules (try `seraphim check`):
# הבא☀ is a "bright" consonant, and אלוקים☀ פדב puts two vowels together.

@title: Never, from the far past onward, have I comprehended it: the allure of Aghma Shwa
@tense: nonpast

word nonpast                       # PRO:T / t / NEG / PRO:V
  top: אלוקים הבא☀
  1:   Ø
  2:   הדסא חכּז☀
  end: אלוקים☢ אלוקים

